Released {{ .Chart.Name }}-{{ .Chart.Version }} as {{ .Release.Name }} in namespace {{ .Release.Namespace }}.

{{- if .Values.image.digest }}
Image: {{ .Values.image.repository }}@{{ .Values.image.digest }}
{{- else }}
Image: {{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag | default .Chart.AppVersion }}
{{- end }}

{{- if not .Values.image.repository }}

WARNING: image.repository is empty, so the pods cannot pull an image. Set it to
the image your CI pushes, e.g.

    --set image.repository=ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>
{{- end }}

Reach it:
{{- if .Values.ingress.enabled }}
{{- range $host := .Values.ingress.hosts }}
{{- range .paths }}
  http{{ if $.Values.ingress.tls }}s{{ end }}://{{ $host.host }}{{ .path }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
<<- if .ServesGRPCIngress>>
{{- if .Values.grpcIngress.enabled }}
{{- range $host := .Values.grpcIngress.hosts }}
  {{ $host.host }}:443 (gRPC, TLS terminated at the ingress)
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
<<- end>>
{{- if not (or .Values.ingress.enabled <<if .ServesGRPCIngress>>.Values.grpcIngress.enabled<<else>>false<<end>>) }}
  kubectl -n {{ .Release.Namespace }} port-forward svc/{{ include "<<.Identifier>>.fullname" . }} <<if .ServesHTTP>>{{ .Values.service.httpPort }}:{{ .Values.service.httpPort }}<<else>>{{ .Values.service.grpcPort }}:{{ .Values.service.grpcPort }}<<end>>
{{- end }}

Two things this chart does NOT create; both must already exist or the pods will
not start:

1. The credentials file, on every node that can schedule this app:

       <<.HelmConfig.CredentialsHostPath>>/<<.HelmConfigDirName>>/prod.yaml

   It is the second entry in CONFIG and overrides the image's own base.yaml, so
   it is where the real `db` block belongs (host, port, user, pswd, driver) plus
   any secrets. Without it the app exits with "db configuration not found".

   It is deliberately not a Secret or ConfigMap: Helm stores release values in
   the cluster, where `helm get values` would print them back.

   NOTE: editing that file does not restart anything — nothing in the release
   changes. Bump the chart version to roll the pods.

2. The image pull secret{{ range .Values.imagePullSecrets }} "{{ .name }}"{{ end }}, since ghcr.io packages are private by default:

       kubectl -n {{ .Release.Namespace }} create secret docker-registry ghcr-login-secret \
         --docker-server=ghcr.io --docker-username=<user> --docker-password=<token>

Check status:

    kubectl -n {{ .Release.Namespace }} rollout status deploy/{{ include "<<.Identifier>>.fullname" . }}
